  "content": {
    "title": "'American Idol' reveals its Top 14 after eliminations",
    "text": "March 30, 2026Updated March 31, 2026, 5:41 p.m. ETIt's an \"American Idol\" plot twist so unexpected, even host Ryan Seacrest was shocked.After the first audience vote of the season, the reality singing competition was forced to postpone a slated round of eliminations as the final counts were tallied. Though the Top 12 were set to be revealed, only six \"Idol\" hopefuls went home, leaving the Top 14 in the running. The final two eliminations will officially be unveiled on April 6.\"To ensure complete accuracy with the numbers, I was literally just told we are not going to announce eliminations tonight,\" Seacrest said as the panel of judges, which includes Carrie Underwood, Lionel Richie and Luke Bryan, reacted in shock.During the March 30 \"Songs of Faith\" episode, for the first time, the singers' fates were not in the hands of judges. The votes were tallied from viewers' texts, online submissions and social media comments based on the Top 20's \"ohana week\" performances.\"This is the first time it's ever happened. Believe me, I've been here every night,\" Seacrest continued. \"We want to make sure we get every vote counted, and every vote right. We'll carry forward those votes, get everything verified.\"The longtime host of the show said the delay came in part because they had opened voting up through new avenues, leading to a deluge of responses. Seacrest said, \"tens of millions of votes [were] coming in at a rate we've never seen before. Truly unprecedented.\"The episode was the first time this season that the celebrity judges took the stage themselves, with Richie and Bryan opening the show with \"Jesus Is Love,\" performed alongside the Top 20 contestants. Later, Underwood sang \"How Great Thou Art\" – which she'd also performed during last year's \"Songs of Faith\" episode.Here's who stayed and who went home.Who's in the 'American Idol' Top 14 in 2026?Philmon LeeBraden RumfeltJake ThistleJesse FindlingLucas LeonHannah HarperChris TungsethJulián KalelRaeDaniel StallworthKeyla RichardsonJordan McCulloughBrooks RosserKyndal InskeepWho was sent home on 'American Idol?'AbayomiMakiyahMadison MoonRuby RaeGenevieve HeywardKutter Bradley",
